{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1778109850,"nonce":"u1p/PNW2flhD7BklT/t9s7S4DJU=","message":"## Idea: constraint-based issue generation\n\nBeyond pure scaffolding (Option A: \\`mandible project init --template ...\\`), the templating mechanism could support **constraints on issue creation**: certain issue *types* (or any issue, depending on the policy) require being filed/cross-referenced in specified coordination issues at creation time.\n\nE.g., an \"analysis\" issue type could require:\n- Filing as an issue with \\`feature\\` label.\n- Auto-comment (or interactive prompt) on the project's analyses coordination issue.\n- Possibly also a comment on phases coord if a phase is currently active.\n\nOther types could have different constraint sets (training-method issue → comment on training-methods coord; cross-project concern → comment on meta coord).\n\nMechanism could be CLI-level (\\`mandible issue new --type analysis\\` enforces the constraints) or post-hoc check (\\`mandible issue lint\\` validates that issues of a given type have the required cross-refs).\n\nKeep this in mind when designing the templating feature — the template defines not just the coordination issues themselves but also the constraint rules that govern what gets auto-filed-where.\n\n(Brief / general note; will return to this when the feature is being designed.)","files":null}]}